# Vercel build config for this monorepo.
#
# IMPORTANT: In your Vercel project settings, set the Root Directory to `web`.
# That isolates the build to this subdirectory, so the Python engine, the
# licensed java_files/ oracle, docs/, tests/, and other parent-repo artifacts
# are never uploaded or built by Vercel.
#
# With Root Directory = web, this file is mostly belt-and-suspenders: the entries
# below guard against local-only artifacts accidentally entering the build context.

# Local env (never deploy real secrets; Vercel env vars are configured in the dashboard)
.env
.env.local
.env*.local

# Dependencies / build output (Vercel installs + builds fresh)
node_modules
.next
out

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
